  "notes": "Battery-powered 10-input mixer (from the panel drawing and specifications). Channels 1-2: XLR MIC, balanced 6.35 mm LINE IN and an unbalanced TRS insert (INS). Channels 3/4, 5/6, 7/8: XLR MIC plus a stereo line pair (L works as MONO). IN 9/10 is a stereo line pair; REC/STREAM IN/OUT are RCA. MAIN OUT is balanced TRS; MON SEND, FX SEND and PHONES are unbalanced TRS. The insert path is not modelled. DC input not listed. Controls from the Quick Start Guide, 'Step 2: Controls' (1-12) and its panel drawing: channels 1 and 2 with GAIN, PAN, MON, 3-band EQ (LOW/MID/HIGH), FX and channel fader; channels 3/4, 5/6 and 7/8 with separate MIC and LINE gain, BAL, MON, EQ, FX and fader; channel 9/10 with LINE gain, BAL, MON, EQ, FX and fader; PHANTOM (all XLR mic inputs), MON SEND and FX SEND masters, PHONES and the MAIN fader. The REC/STREAM input has no controls on the panel. Assumptions: the headphones and REC/STREAM OUT carry the main mix; faders and levels at MIN are silent; whether the MAIN fader also sets the headphones is not stated (modelled: no).",
